The value is already backslash-escaped, and the Ninja generator escapes it a
second time, so gcc receives -DSAMBA_PACKAGE_NAME="\\\"samba\\\"" and chokes on
the stray backslash in sambausershareplugin.cpp ("missing terminating "
character" / "stray '\' in program").  Let CMake hold the quoted value and let
Ninja do the shell escaping, as verified with Ninja + gcc.

--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -149,3 +149,3 @@
 if(NOT SAMBA_PACKAGE_NAME)
-    set(SAMBA_PACKAGE_NAME \\\"samba\\\")
+    set(SAMBA_PACKAGE_NAME "\"samba\"")
 endif(NOT SAMBA_PACKAGE_NAME)
